& [Delineation]
  + scripted provider envelopes are deterministic test inputs generated by Cantor and not model outputs
  + orchestration orders already verified pure functions and does not authorize a transport or process adapter
  + complete report proof and stopped report proof are different paths because a terminal head cannot honestly be represented as live READY reentry
  + this slice therefore admits only a fully supplied exact complete fixture and fails without constructing a partial report

& [SelectedFlow]
  + validate opening policy model prompt and caller-supplied ordered unique fixture call identifiers
  + construct the next provider request then synthesize its exact one-call response envelope
  + run one deterministic advancement and admit the joined IterationRecord
  + continue from the exact returned READY registry and head or stop iteration at terminal
  + refuse unused or insufficient scripted call identifiers
  + construct terminal reflection request synthesize its exact identity-bound response assemble IterativeReport and validate the wrapper

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty marks all generated provider envelopes as fixture evidence and sets provider_execution_claimed false
  + Security validates the final successor registry by exact INSPECT and READ against terminal observation
  + Planner bounds the loop by RunPolicy and the finite call-identifier script
  + Weaver validates full request response tool projection and handle order through Slice3 prefix replay
  + Scribe retains the complete report reflection request sanitized response and exact final registry
  + Refiner keeps exact registry state outside every synthesized provider request
  + Observer admits the wrapper only after IterativeReport prefix reflection final-output registry and nonclaim validators agree

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated scripted_orchestrator forms runner validator deterministic fixture and tests
  + keep stopped orchestration real provider transport process timing filesystem persistence and all external effects locked

& [Rollback]
  + additive module exports and tests remove cleanly without changing predecessor behavior or data
